module test.claim.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_witness

import tools.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_transport {
  slbu_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds
}

// Seed-unavailable self-host behavioral receipt for dag/std/logic.dag (Control (b)):
// tools.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_transport emits dag/std/logic.dag via the
// real gunbc binary, compiles the emitted Rust with standard infrastructure deps
// (im, serde, etc. -- required by v1_rt.rs which the emitter includes unconditionally)
// but WITHOUT the seed crate v1-compiler, and runs the resulting witness binary to
// prove the emitted logic module executes without seed dependency.
//
// SEED-DEPENDENCY BOUNDARY: the control denies three of four modes:
//   (1) EXECUTION: the emitted binary runs without the seed binary
//   (2) LINKAGE: v1-compiler absent at cargo build time
//   (3) FALLBACK: no runtime fallback to v1-compiler
//   (4) EMBEDDED SOURCE: v1_rt.rs present (unconditional emitter behavior) -- the
//       transport checks via per-subject spelling search: emitted .rs files are read
//       and checked for `v1_compiler::` tokens (seed crate namespace); a match refuses the
//       receipt (validator, not construction; the structural proof is the absent v1-compiler
//       dependency in the manifest).
//
// THIS IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR CONTROL (a). Control (b) tests whether the candidate
// depends on the seed; control (a) tests whether the comparison discriminates. Neither
// establishes the other, and a green (b) does not cover a missing (a).
//
// CLASSIFIED onto LocalRepoWetLane: effects confined to temp dir + cargo build with
// standard cached deps, no network required, same class as existing local git repo
// operations on that lane. Hermetic envelope refuses because shell.Mktemp.Dir,
// Filesystem.Write, cargo.Build.BuildManifest, and gunbc.WitnessBin.Run have no
// mock_response.

test fn self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds() -> Bool {
  slbu_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds()
}
